WEBVTT

00:00:01.900 --> 00:00:11.990
Please don't expect too much from it.
This story is a simple illustration of the three
Minami sisters and the ordinary life they lead.

00:00:16.630 --> 00:00:17.910
It's winter!

00:00:18.430 --> 00:00:20.290
Time for the kotatsu!

00:00:23.110 --> 00:00:25.350
It's so warm...

00:00:25.350 --> 00:00:28.540
Man, kotatsus are great.

00:00:29.170 --> 00:00:31.930
This must be what Heaven is like.

00:00:32.390 --> 00:00:35.430
You can't get out once you're in.

00:00:35.430 --> 00:00:38.930
I think I'll just live under here.

00:00:40.430 --> 00:00:45.690
Sensei!

00:00:47.690 --> 00:00:48.690
Sensei...
Ninomiya-kun...

00:00:55.140 --> 00:00:56.590
So warm...

00:00:56.590 --> 00:00:59.030
This is paradise.

00:02:39.010 --> 00:02:43.010
We Started Living Green

00:02:44.020 --> 00:02:46.580
I'm pretty sure we need lights.

00:02:46.580 --> 00:02:49.180
We can't do anything like this.

00:02:52.450 --> 00:02:54.520
Okay. They're on.

00:02:54.520 --> 00:02:56.530
Okay. Thank you.

00:02:56.530 --> 00:03:00.030
Why did you turn off the lights?

00:03:00.030 --> 00:03:04.290
Keiko, what can we do to be greener? More eco-friendly?

00:03:04.290 --> 00:03:05.790
Eco-friendly?

00:03:05.790 --> 00:03:10.040
Is that why the kotatsu is unplugged?

00:03:10.040 --> 00:03:11.800
Precisely.

00:03:11.800 --> 00:03:15.180
Our electric bill last month
.was happier than a kite.

00:03:15.180 --> 00:03:17.720
That's why we're making a special effort to be eco-friendly this month.

00:03:17.720 --> 00:03:20.990
Oh, so you're economizing.

00:03:23.190 --> 00:03:27.470
It's not about economizing.
It's about the environment, Mako-chan.

00:03:30.040 --> 00:03:31.700
R-Right.

00:03:32.310 --> 00:03:33.780
Okay!

00:03:34.440 --> 00:03:38.860
Sitting inside a kotatsu that's turned off is worse than not sitting in one at all.

00:03:38.860 --> 00:03:42.290
Keiko, do you have any ideas on how we can be more eco-friendly?

00:03:42.290 --> 00:03:44.440
Even if it only makes a small difference.

00:03:44.440 --> 00:03:47.740
With enough small differences,
we can save the Earth!

00:03:47.740 --> 00:03:49.900
Let's see...

00:03:51.590 --> 00:03:57.000
Sometimes, when a pen runs out of ink,
you can fix it by breathing on it.

00:03:57.000 --> 00:03:58.630
Really?

00:04:05.350 --> 00:04:08.720
I happen to have such a pen right here.

00:04:09.880 --> 00:04:13.390
Why didn't you just throw
it away when it ran out?

00:04:13.390 --> 00:04:15.720
Because Haruka is chea—

00:04:17.030 --> 00:04:19.060
Stare...

00:04:19.570 --> 00:04:23.960
Because Haruka is such an
.environmentally conscious girl.

00:04:23.960 --> 00:04:25.490
Okay!

00:04:26.710 --> 00:04:28.530
It doesn't work.

00:04:29.870 --> 00:04:32.160
Let's see it, then.

00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:33.330
O-Okay...

00:04:40.130 --> 00:04:41.970
Eco-friendly

00:04:41.970 --> 00:04:43.010
See?
Eco-friendly

00:04:49.270 --> 00:04:49.550
<b>Eco-friendly</b>

00:04:49.550 --> 00:04:51.660
You just wasted ink and paper!

00:04:51.660 --> 00:04:53.880
What's eco-friendly about that?!

00:04:55.700 --> 00:04:58.960
Can't you think of something
that's a bit more efficient?

00:04:58.960 --> 00:05:00.720
Oh, I know!

00:05:04.530 --> 00:05:08.070
Two people can share a
blanket to warm each other up.

00:05:09.690 --> 00:05:13.040
That's the ultimate form of energy
conservation: using body heat!

00:05:14.390 --> 00:05:16.750
Keiko. Do you get cold easily?

00:05:16.750 --> 00:05:18.540
Y-Yes...

00:05:18.910 --> 00:05:21.170
You're a menace to the environment!

00:05:24.920 --> 00:05:27.700
Mako-chan, let's wrap ourselves up.

00:05:27.700 --> 00:05:29.970
I-I'm okay like this.

00:05:35.290 --> 00:05:40.110
You're so warm, Mako-chan.

00:05:40.910 --> 00:05:43.240
I-I...

00:05:43.240 --> 00:05:44.110
I?

00:05:44.510 --> 00:05:46.990
I gotta go! It's getting dark!

00:05:46.990 --> 00:05:48.410
Bye!

00:05:52.150 --> 00:05:53.620
Mako-chan...

00:05:56.620 --> 00:06:00.960
Our eco-friendly friends have left us.

00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:02.210
Well then.

00:06:03.280 --> 00:06:04.710
What are you doing?

00:06:05.110 --> 00:06:10.470
I'll help out Haruka-neesama while warming myself up at the stove.

00:06:10.850 --> 00:06:13.430
I-Incredible eco-IQ!

00:06:13.970 --> 00:06:15.250
Okay, then. Me too.

00:06:15.250 --> 00:06:18.580
I'll help myself to a sneak preview of dinner while warming myself up over the rice cooker's steam!

00:06:20.520 --> 00:06:24.320
Man, having a nice, warm
kotatsu sure feels good!

00:06:24.320 --> 00:06:26.740
We can turn it on while
we're eating dinner, at least.

00:06:26.740 --> 00:06:29.740
I'm starting to see you as the
Goddess of the Kotatsu!

00:06:30.840 --> 00:06:33.740
Thank you, Haruka-neesama.

00:06:34.640 --> 00:06:36.330
Okay, time to eat.

00:06:36.770 --> 00:06:39.040
Let's dig in!

00:06:48.510 --> 00:06:51.090
Thank you for the food.

00:06:55.310 --> 00:06:58.640
She really <i>did</i> mean just during dinner.

00:06:58.640 --> 00:07:00.300
Well then.

00:07:00.300 --> 00:07:02.650
You'd better take your baths
.before the water gets cold.

00:07:02.650 --> 00:07:05.800
But there's still some heat left in the kotatsu...

00:07:05.800 --> 00:07:07.690
You're not allowed to run any more hot water.

00:07:08.530 --> 00:07:10.620
I'll go in first!

00:07:16.050 --> 00:07:19.410
Oh, did Kana beat you to it?

00:07:20.830 --> 00:07:24.800
Haruka-neesama, your
.hands look really cold.

00:07:24.800 --> 00:07:28.420
I used cold water instead of hot water to wash the dishes this time.

00:07:30.350 --> 00:07:32.340
Haruka-neesama...

00:07:32.340 --> 00:07:35.380
Your consideration for the
environment is truly admirable.

00:07:35.380 --> 00:07:37.930
You truly are the Green Goddess!

00:07:39.610 --> 00:07:43.440
I'll do everything I can to make
.our home more eco-friendly.

00:07:46.350 --> 00:07:48.150
You left the shower on!

00:07:48.150 --> 00:07:49.900
Dry your hair quicker!

00:07:51.070 --> 00:07:55.280
You're only allowed one-third of a cup of water for brushing your teeth!

00:07:55.280 --> 00:07:57.520
Fine, but you better do the same.

00:07:57.520 --> 00:07:59.200
I'll be watching!

00:08:00.840 --> 00:08:02.700
It's not turned on.

00:08:02.700 --> 00:08:04.960
I'll catch a cold like this.

00:08:05.630 --> 00:08:08.220
You can borrow my blanket.

00:08:08.920 --> 00:08:10.780
Oh, thanks!

00:08:10.780 --> 00:08:13.930
I'm so lucky to have a sister who
.looks out for me. Ecologically.

00:08:13.940 --> 00:08:16.670
It's almost time for this
.year's Loincloth Festival.

00:08:16.670 --> 00:08:19.720
It sure is. We've got a lot of people
participating in the festival every year,

00:08:19.720 --> 00:08:22.030
but this year, we've got especially many full families participating.

00:08:22.030 --> 00:08:24.430
I guess I'll sleep early.
For the environment's sake.

00:08:24.430 --> 00:08:25.090
I'm participating in it this year too!
I guess I'll sleep early.
For the environment's sake.

00:08:25.090 --> 00:08:26.430
Yeah.
I'm participating in it this year too!

00:08:26.430 --> 00:08:28.780
Kana, give me back the blanket.
So that's why you're only wearing a loincloth today?

00:08:28.780 --> 00:08:28.860
Yeah! I can't wait! I'm ready!
Kana, give me back the blanket.

00:08:28.860 --> 00:08:31.720
Yeah! I can't wait! I'm ready!

00:08:31.720 --> 00:08:34.180
N-No way...

00:08:34.180 --> 00:08:39.500
Was this all because she didn't want to be cold when she got into bed?

00:08:39.500 --> 00:08:42.250
She lent me this blanket just
so I'd warm it up for her?

00:08:44.210 --> 00:08:46.960
What an evil eco-genius!

00:08:50.520 --> 00:08:52.980
Wanna sleep together tonight, Chiaki?

00:08:52.980 --> 00:08:53.740
Huh?

00:09:12.610 --> 00:09:14.140
What?

00:09:14.140 --> 00:09:15.490
Chiaki's not coming today?

00:09:15.490 --> 00:09:17.840
She caught a cold.

00:09:17.840 --> 00:09:19.300
Oh, come on!

00:09:19.300 --> 00:09:22.120
We were supposed to
have a snack party today!

00:09:22.120 --> 00:09:23.980
What's a snack party?

00:09:23.980 --> 00:09:26.440
It's like a party with snacks.

00:09:26.440 --> 00:09:27.960
Yo, Yoshino!

00:09:27.960 --> 00:09:29.520
Is Chiaki here?

00:09:29.520 --> 00:09:30.640
Oh, Touma.

00:09:30.640 --> 00:09:33.210
Chiaki's off sick today with a cold.

00:09:33.930 --> 00:09:36.880
What'll happen to the snack party, then?

00:09:37.370 --> 00:09:40.900
Unfortunately, it looks like we'll need to
.take a rain check on that snack party.

00:09:40.900 --> 00:09:42.200
What the heck, Makoto?

00:09:42.200 --> 00:09:44.270
You weren't even invited.

00:09:44.270 --> 00:09:47.140
The party will be held at a
.later date, and I'll be there.

00:09:47.140 --> 00:09:49.980
Don't just invite yourself!
Who died and made you boss?!

00:09:50.470 --> 00:09:53.980
In any case, we need Chiaki
.to get better soon.

00:09:55.450 --> 00:09:59.300
That's right. Don't they say
egg sake is good for a cold?

00:09:59.300 --> 00:10:01.410
We drink egg sake whenever
.we catch colds in our family.

00:10:02.410 --> 00:10:04.220
What's egg sake?

00:10:04.220 --> 00:10:05.790
Sake mixed with eggs.

00:10:05.790 --> 00:10:07.910
Sake?!

00:10:07.910 --> 00:10:09.680
But Chiaki's underage!

00:10:09.680 --> 00:10:11.080
Whoa, he looks serious!

00:10:11.750 --> 00:10:16.560
I think people make an exception
.for egg sake when you have a cold.

00:10:16.560 --> 00:10:18.760
I mean, don't you drink sweet
sake at the Doll Festival?

00:10:20.000 --> 00:10:21.700
The Doll Festival...

00:10:22.340 --> 00:10:24.010
I'm a guy, so I don't drink!

00:10:24.010 --> 00:10:24.420
What does that have to do with anything?

00:10:24.420 --> 00:10:25.900
What else is good for a cold?

00:10:25.900 --> 00:10:27.100
Do you think a true man like me would actually participate in the Doll Festival?

00:10:27.100 --> 00:10:28.790
Udon's easy to digest
when you're sick, right?

00:10:28.790 --> 00:10:30.960
"True man," my ass! You're just a wimp!
Udon's easy to digest
when you're sick, right?

00:10:30.960 --> 00:10:31.520
Boiled tofu is pretty easy to eat too.
"True man," my ass! You're just a wimp!

00:10:31.520 --> 00:10:33.630
Oh yeah? Then <i>you're</i> just an idiot!
Boiled tofu is pretty easy to eat too.

00:10:33.630 --> 00:10:35.200
And it's nutritious.

00:10:35.200 --> 00:10:37.400
If it's nutrition you want,
look no further than meat!

00:10:37.400 --> 00:10:40.360
Can you actually eat meat when you're sick?

00:10:40.360 --> 00:10:41.430
What did you just say?

00:10:41.430 --> 00:10:42.780
You wanna go?

00:10:45.510 --> 00:10:48.850
All right! Let's pay her
a visit with some food!

00:10:48.850 --> 00:10:49.790
Yeah.

00:10:53.710 --> 00:10:56.260
We brought today's handouts for Chiaki.

00:10:56.260 --> 00:10:58.690
Oh my, thank you for
.coming all the way here.

00:10:58.690 --> 00:11:00.470
It's been a while,
hasn't it, Makoto-kun?

00:11:00.470 --> 00:11:02.050
Yes, Haruka-san.

00:11:02.050 --> 00:11:04.940
Huh? Don't you come
here all the time?

00:11:07.010 --> 00:11:10.340
Come on! It's Mako-chan who's always here, remember?

00:11:10.340 --> 00:11:12.040
Oh, right!

00:11:12.040 --> 00:11:13.730
They're so alike.

00:11:16.490 --> 00:11:18.450
I brought some delicious tofu.

00:11:18.450 --> 00:11:18.590
Udon
I brought some delicious tofu.

00:11:18.590 --> 00:11:18.700
I brought some delicious udon.
Udon

00:11:18.700 --> 00:11:20.610
Udon
I brought some delicious udon.

00:11:20.970 --> 00:11:22.620
Thank you.

00:11:23.190 --> 00:11:26.240
I brought some delicious eggs.

00:11:26.240 --> 00:11:27.700
Gave up on the sake, though.

00:11:28.650 --> 00:11:30.000
This is from Natsuki.

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:31.590
He says these leeks
are really high quality.

00:11:31.590 --> 00:11:33.000
From Natsuki-kun, you say?

00:11:33.000 --> 00:11:34.490
Thanks.

00:11:34.490 --> 00:11:35.840
Tell him thanks for me as well.

00:11:35.840 --> 00:11:37.370
Got it.

00:11:37.370 --> 00:11:38.350
Leeks?

00:11:38.350 --> 00:11:40.400
How are leeks good for a cold?

00:11:41.590 --> 00:11:44.800
Didn't people used to say that?

00:11:44.800 --> 00:11:47.430
You know, that wrapping a leek around your throat's good for a cold?

00:11:48.250 --> 00:11:50.730
A leek around your throat?

00:11:50.730 --> 00:11:53.260
What are you saying?

00:11:53.260 --> 00:11:59.070
Quit making me sound crazy just because you lack common knowledge!

00:11:59.790 --> 00:12:03.700
I brought meat, Haruka-san!

00:12:03.700 --> 00:12:05.760
Oh, marbled beef!

00:12:05.760 --> 00:12:06.700
Thank you.

00:12:07.140 --> 00:12:09.000
You really brought some?

00:12:09.000 --> 00:12:10.480
What an idiot.

00:12:10.480 --> 00:12:12.430
You're the idiot, you stupid leek nut!

00:12:12.430 --> 00:12:15.920
You're the real idiot for not knowing about the healing properties of leeks!

00:12:16.510 --> 00:12:18.460
So you really want a piece of me, huh?

00:12:18.460 --> 00:12:19.670
You're on!

00:12:23.510 --> 00:12:25.060
I'm home.

00:12:28.370 --> 00:12:30.220
What's going on here?

00:12:30.220 --> 00:12:32.370
Welcome home, Kana.

00:12:32.370 --> 00:12:35.400
They all came to see Chiaki.

00:12:35.400 --> 00:12:35.540
Udon
They all came to see Chiaki.

00:12:35.540 --> 00:12:35.570
Udon

00:12:35.570 --> 00:12:38.320
marbled beef
Udon

00:12:38.320 --> 00:12:38.700
marbled beef

00:12:41.910 --> 00:12:44.700
With all this... I think I know
.what dinner's gonna be.

00:12:50.290 --> 00:12:52.340
I'm feeling a lot better.

00:12:53.920 --> 00:12:55.710
This smell...

00:12:57.150 --> 00:12:59.210
Are you awake?

00:13:03.430 --> 00:13:07.070
We're having sukiyaki tonight, thanks to you!

00:13:07.070 --> 00:13:08.920
Sukiyaki?!

00:13:14.480 --> 00:13:16.150
Hey, Chiaki!

00:13:16.150 --> 00:13:18.080
We're having a sukiyaki party tonight!

00:13:18.080 --> 00:13:20.140
What? Why are we having a party?

00:13:34.230 --> 00:13:35.820
Hey. Good evening.

00:13:37.030 --> 00:13:39.290
Welcome, Uncle Takeru.

00:13:39.890 --> 00:13:42.800
Huh? Isn't this room a bit cold?

00:13:42.800 --> 00:13:44.260
So you've noticed.

00:13:44.260 --> 00:13:46.440
We're back to living chea—

00:13:47.970 --> 00:13:49.640
Living green, right?

00:13:49.640 --> 00:13:50.990
Right, Takeru!

00:13:50.990 --> 00:13:52.360
Take us out for dinner!

00:13:53.230 --> 00:13:56.540
You're always coming
.here to eat, after all.

00:13:56.540 --> 00:13:58.280
I guess you're right.

00:13:58.280 --> 00:13:59.780
It <i>is</i> a bit cold here.

00:13:59.780 --> 00:14:01.880
Let's go eat out tonight.

00:14:01.880 --> 00:14:02.660
Yes!

00:14:04.230 --> 00:14:05.990
What do you all feel like?

00:14:05.990 --> 00:14:07.810
I feel like meat.

00:14:07.810 --> 00:14:10.480
We just had a sukiyaki party a few days ago.

00:14:10.480 --> 00:14:12.490
Huh? You had a sukiyaki party?

00:14:12.930 --> 00:14:15.400
Why didn't you invite me?

00:14:15.400 --> 00:14:17.150
I'm pretty good at making soup...

00:14:17.150 --> 00:14:18.300
What should we eat then?
I'm pretty good at making soup...

00:14:18.300 --> 00:14:19.090
What should we eat then?

00:14:19.090 --> 00:14:21.170
I wanna eat some fish.

00:14:21.570 --> 00:14:23.620
At times like these...

00:14:25.170 --> 00:14:26.670
I know just where we can go!

00:14:27.420 --> 00:14:31.680
Fukuya          Bar & Grill

00:14:31.680 --> 00:14:34.680
Rice
Grilled Chicken (salt
Whole & Filleted Fish
Deep Fryer
A La Carte
Appetizers

00:14:34.680 --> 00:14:36.950
Looks good!

00:14:36.950 --> 00:14:39.310
Do you come here often?

00:14:39.310 --> 00:14:40.440
Every once in a while.

00:14:47.420 --> 00:14:49.110
Haruka-neesama.

00:14:49.110 --> 00:14:51.620
What's "namakuchiko"?

00:14:51.620 --> 00:14:54.540
Salted sea cucumber innards, I think.

00:14:54.540 --> 00:14:56.360
Then what's "hachinoko"?

00:14:56.360 --> 00:14:58.500
I think those are baby bees.

00:15:02.020 --> 00:15:04.380
Would you like to order?

00:15:04.380 --> 00:15:07.260
You should just have some
.grilled chicken or something.

00:15:07.260 --> 00:15:08.550
Grilled chicken...

00:15:08.550 --> 00:15:10.340
Liver
Heart
Cartilage
Gizzard
Skin
Thigh
Underbelly
Neck

00:15:10.340 --> 00:15:12.550
Underbelly
Thigh
Skin
Gizzard
Cartilage
Heart
Liver

00:15:16.350 --> 00:15:19.940
I know it's not on the menu, but would you happen to have salisbury steak?

00:15:20.390 --> 00:15:21.610
We do.

00:15:21.610 --> 00:15:22.970
You do?!

00:15:22.970 --> 00:15:24.360
Doesn't hurt to ask, huh?

00:15:25.030 --> 00:15:28.360
Well, you two feel free to
.order anything you'd like.

00:15:28.360 --> 00:15:31.450
Do you have any recommendations?

00:15:31.450 --> 00:15:35.200
Well, you <i>have</i> to try the beef
.tendon stew here at least once.

00:15:35.200 --> 00:15:38.390
I'm sorry, we're out of beef tendons today.

00:15:38.390 --> 00:15:40.040
We do have offal stew, though.

00:15:40.040 --> 00:15:42.370
I'll have that, then.

00:15:42.370 --> 00:15:44.040
Excuse me.

00:15:44.040 --> 00:15:46.580
Sardines, mullet roe,
pickled tuna, goosefish liver!

00:15:46.580 --> 00:15:47.630
Whoa, Kana!

00:15:47.630 --> 00:15:49.440
Are you brewing some kind of potion?!

00:15:58.740 --> 00:16:00.140
Delicious!

00:16:00.640 --> 00:16:02.640
This salisbury steak is excellent.

00:16:02.640 --> 00:16:04.400
Good work, Takeru!

00:16:04.400 --> 00:16:05.400
Is it?

00:16:05.400 --> 00:16:07.150
Well, I'm glad they had it, then.

00:16:07.150 --> 00:16:11.650
These go well with the rice,
...but I definitely need...

00:16:13.630 --> 00:16:17.240
Takeru, can I have some?
Just a bit of the foam?

00:16:17.240 --> 00:16:18.240
No can do.

00:16:18.830 --> 00:16:21.620
This offal stew is really good!

00:16:21.620 --> 00:16:22.660
Really?

00:16:22.660 --> 00:16:25.100
Maybe them running out of beef
.tendons wasn't such a bad thing.

00:16:26.630 --> 00:16:28.000
Wanna order something else?

00:16:28.000 --> 00:16:29.220
Yeah!

00:16:29.870 --> 00:16:31.570
Excuse me!

00:16:31.570 --> 00:16:32.560
Yes?

00:16:33.590 --> 00:16:35.640
Do you happen to have rice omelets?

00:16:35.640 --> 00:16:36.620
We do.

00:16:37.260 --> 00:16:39.220
Looks like you've got
.everything but beef tendons.

00:16:39.770 --> 00:16:43.180
Excuse me, do you have any
recommendations today?

00:16:43.180 --> 00:16:46.100
So much for <i>my</i> recommendations...
Our pickled mackerel and cheese chijimi are good today.

00:16:46.510 --> 00:16:49.070
Do you have any refreshing,
wheat-based drinks?

00:16:49.070 --> 00:16:50.940
Potato-based is fine too.

00:16:50.940 --> 00:16:52.530
I don't think either one
.of those is fine for <i>you</i>.

00:16:56.470 --> 00:16:58.200
That was good.

00:16:58.200 --> 00:17:00.450
I'll be out like a light the moment I get home.

00:17:00.990 --> 00:17:03.000
Good, you say?

00:17:03.000 --> 00:17:07.960
I'm afraid you still don't fully appreciate
.the beauty of the bar and grill.

00:17:07.960 --> 00:17:08.880
Huh?

00:17:09.270 --> 00:17:13.420
The longer you stay,
the better it tastes!

00:17:16.110 --> 00:17:17.930
I see.

00:17:17.930 --> 00:17:20.720
Well, the night is still young.

00:17:20.720 --> 00:17:21.720
All right!

00:17:21.720 --> 00:17:24.850
We'll keep you company tonight, Takeru!

00:17:24.850 --> 00:17:26.400
That's the spirit, Chiaki!

00:17:26.400 --> 00:17:27.480
Keep ordering!

00:17:27.480 --> 00:17:29.310
Excuse me!

00:17:31.460 --> 00:17:32.320
Yes?

00:17:33.590 --> 00:17:36.150
Do you have anything a bit more exotic?

00:17:36.150 --> 00:17:38.370
Do you have anything like pudding?

00:17:38.370 --> 00:17:40.330
Do you have any other recommendations?

00:17:40.330 --> 00:17:42.420
Do you accept credit card?

00:18:04.490 --> 00:18:06.980
Oh, Mako-chan. Welcome.

00:18:07.330 --> 00:18:09.770
Are those your pajamas?

00:18:09.770 --> 00:18:11.060
Did you just wake up?

00:18:11.060 --> 00:18:11.730
No.

00:18:11.730 --> 00:18:13.980
I've been awake for quite a while.

00:18:23.080 --> 00:18:25.620
Hello, Haruka-san.

00:18:26.680 --> 00:18:33.000
At our morning meeting, we decided to have a pajama day.

00:18:33.000 --> 00:18:34.420
A pajama day?!

00:18:34.830 --> 00:18:37.880
We're allowed to spend the whole day in our pajamas today.

00:18:37.880 --> 00:18:41.350
Oh, you can be lazy for a whole day?

00:18:41.350 --> 00:18:44.430
That's nice and all, but where's Kana?

00:18:44.430 --> 00:18:45.350
Dunno.

00:18:45.350 --> 00:18:49.810
Kana called me here, but
...she's nowhere to be seen...

00:18:49.810 --> 00:18:51.310
There you have it.

00:18:51.310 --> 00:18:54.040
You should kill some time with us instead.

00:18:54.040 --> 00:18:58.280
What am I gonna do without Kana if I come close to blowing my cover?

00:18:59.700 --> 00:19:01.420
Oh, I know!

00:19:01.420 --> 00:19:05.160
It's not like I'm trying to hide it,
so I have nothing to fear!

00:19:05.160 --> 00:19:06.960
Oh, Mako-chan.

00:19:08.310 --> 00:19:09.940
Welcome.

00:19:15.650 --> 00:19:18.130
Do you want to borrow a pair of pajamas?

00:19:18.540 --> 00:19:19.970
No, thank you!

00:19:19.970 --> 00:19:21.010
Really?

00:19:21.010 --> 00:19:23.550
You should join us.

00:19:23.550 --> 00:19:28.380
Chiaki, shouldn't you ask
Haruka-san to button up?

00:19:29.090 --> 00:19:33.230
We only have girls coming
here today, so who cares?

00:19:33.230 --> 00:19:34.400
But...

00:19:37.500 --> 00:19:39.320
Hello!

00:19:39.880 --> 00:19:41.320
Welcome.

00:19:41.320 --> 00:19:42.030
Huh?

00:19:42.440 --> 00:19:43.620
What's with the pajamas?

00:19:43.620 --> 00:19:45.030
Did you just wake up?

00:19:45.030 --> 00:19:47.160
We're having a pajama day today.

00:19:48.420 --> 00:19:51.500
How about it? You can
.borrow some of mine.

00:19:59.380 --> 00:20:01.620
It feels like a school trip!

00:20:01.620 --> 00:20:03.510
Wanna have a pillow fight?

00:20:04.780 --> 00:20:07.010
What's wrong, Mako-chan?

00:20:07.700 --> 00:20:09.890
Why don't we get a futon out?

00:20:09.890 --> 00:20:11.850
I have one ready.

00:20:13.650 --> 00:20:17.690
I hung it out in the sun, so it
.should be pretty nice now.

00:20:17.690 --> 00:20:19.650
It's comfy.

00:20:20.690 --> 00:20:23.100
Let's sleep together, Mako-chan.

00:20:23.100 --> 00:20:24.660
Don't be stupid!

00:20:24.660 --> 00:20:26.660
Who're you calling stupid?!

00:20:30.760 --> 00:20:31.720
This is bad...

00:20:31.720 --> 00:20:35.020
If I get pulled into this school
trip mood, it'll be awful!

00:20:35.020 --> 00:20:36.500
I have to do something!

00:20:36.500 --> 00:20:39.660
We should've bought some snacks.

00:20:42.190 --> 00:20:46.300
There's a new sweet shop by the station!

00:20:46.710 --> 00:20:48.310
Let's all go!

00:20:58.870 --> 00:21:02.360
Their sponge cake is lighter than feathers,

00:21:02.360 --> 00:21:04.360
and the cream on it is smoother than silk.

00:21:04.360 --> 00:21:08.870
You'll experience a sweeter dream
than anything you can in your sleep!

00:21:16.070 --> 00:21:18.670
Oh? Haruka started changing.

00:21:18.670 --> 00:21:21.300
I'll wait outside!

00:21:23.670 --> 00:21:24.740
I see.

00:21:24.740 --> 00:21:27.430
Mako-chan wanted to go somewhere.

00:21:27.430 --> 00:21:30.180
She's so young and energetic.

00:21:31.470 --> 00:21:33.180
That was close.

00:21:33.180 --> 00:21:36.190
Where on Earth did Kana go?

00:21:38.440 --> 00:21:39.810
Are you all ready?

00:21:39.810 --> 00:21:41.020
Let's go.

00:21:41.020 --> 00:21:42.690
Okay!

00:21:43.740 --> 00:21:50.660
Sardines, mullet roe,
..pickled tuna, goosefish liver...

00:23:22.170 --> 00:23:24.540
Any plans for Christmas, Atsuko?

00:23:24.540 --> 00:23:25.800
We're having a party at Haruka's place.

00:23:25.800 --> 00:23:26.590
What about you, Maki?

00:23:26.590 --> 00:23:28.630
Having a party at Haruka's place!

00:23:28.630 --> 00:23:32.010
Next episode: "The Goddess Descends on the Holy Night."
